# Line-ending discipline. The installers are bash: if a Windows clone converts
# them to CRLF (Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true), bash dies with
# "$'\r': command not found" on the first line. Forcing LF here overrides any
# local autocrlf setting, so every clone runs on macOS, Linux, WSL, and Git Bash.
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.env.example text eol=lf

# Binary assets, never touched
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.webp binary
*.zip  binary
